    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for sum reduction along a specified dimension. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradReductionSum" kindref="compound">GradReductionSum</ref> class represents the sum reduction operation in the computational graph, computing gradients for summing a tensor along a specific dimension. For the operation <formula id="70">$C = \sum_{i} A_i$</formula> where the sum is taken along dimension <formula id="71">$d$</formula> of tensor <formula id="12">$A$</formula>, the gradient computation follows from:   <formula id="72">\[    \frac{\partial C_j}{\partial A_{j,i}} = 1 \quad \text{for all } i
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="15">$\frac{\partial
L}{\partial C}$</formula> (which has one fewer dimension than the input) must be broadcast along the reduced dimension to match the shape of the input tensor according to the chain rule:    <formula id="73">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A_{j,i}} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C_j}
\quad \text{for all } i
\]</formula></para>
<para>The backward pass broadcasts the incoming gradient along the reduced dimension to restore the original tensor shape, effectively distributing the gradient to all elements that contributed to each sum. This operation is the inverse of the forward sum reduction.</para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves the input tensor from the forward pass to determine the shape for broadcasting the gradient, and stores the dimension along which the reduction was performed.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradMean" kindref="compound">GradMean</ref> for the gradient function for mean reduction. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradBroadcast" kindref="compound">GradBroadcast</ref> for the gradient function for broadcasting operations. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
